    <SkyscannerWidget origin="Dubai" originCode="DXB" destination="New York" destinationCode="JFK" />
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Airlines Flying Nonstop from Dubai to New York</h2>
      <p>Emirates holds a near-monopoly on this route, operating daily nonstop service that is widely regarded as one of the world's best long-haul products.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Emirates</strong> — Daily nonstop from DXB to JFK aboard wide-body aircraft (typically A380 or Boeing 777). The A380 configuration features First Class private suites, Business Class lie-flat beds with in-suite bar, and a generous economy cabin.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What to Expect on a 13.5-Hour Flight</h2>
      <p>At over 13 hours, the Dubai to New York route rewards investment in a premium cabin. Economy is comfortable but long — plan your meals, sleep, and entertainment in advance. Emirates' in-flight entertainment system (ice) is industry-leading with thousands of hours of content.</p>
      <div class="tip-box"><p>The A380 upper deck Business Class cabin is smaller and quieter than the main deck — worth requesting when available. The onboard bar is open to Business and First Class passengers throughout the flight.</p></div>
      <h2>Tips for Dubai to New York Nonstop</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Emirates Skywards miles</strong> can be redeemed for award travel on this route — watch for business class availability, which opens up 30-45 days out.</li>
        <li><strong>Timing matters</strong> — the overnight flight departing DXB in the early morning arrives at JFK in the afternoon, giving you a functional arrival day.</li>
        <li><strong>Visa requirements</strong> — US travellers need ESTA authorization; ensure it is valid before departure from Dubai.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
